# ChatGPT browser-file intake

Store each original browser or ChatGPT Project file under a unique capture
directory together with a manifest recording source project/chat IDs, original
name, MIME type, byte size, SHA-256, acquisition time, source reference, and all
transformations. Include a unique capture nonce and source revision/time so
replays and stale captures can be detected. Never replace original bytes with a
normalized derivative.

Files in this directory are untrusted intake and have no inventory, scientific,
formula, code, or release authority until validated and promoted by Codex.
